#
# Nightly run of the single sign-on watchdog.
#
# cron(8) reads this directory on FreeBSD 13 and later, and it is how the
# OPNsense plugins that schedule anything schedule it. periodic(8) would be the
# other way, but nothing in OPNsense - neither the core package nor any plugin -
# puts anything under /usr/local/etc/periodic. Whether periodic runs at all on a
# given firewall therefore depends on base defaults nobody here maintains, which
# is a poor thing for a watchdog to depend on.
#
# Nothing is written to stdout: the watchdog reports for itself over syslog and
# mail, and cron would send every silent run to root.
SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/etc:/bin:/sbin:/usr/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/local/sbin
#minute	hour	mday	month	wday	who	command
*	*	*	*	*	root	/usr/bin/lockf -t 0 /var/run/openid-connect-refresh.lock /usr/local/sbin/openid-connect-refresh >/dev/null 2>&1
1	3	*	*	*	root	/usr/local/sbin/openid-connect-watch --check >/dev/null 2>&1
